{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "description": "Experimental (`media_buy.execution_requirements`). Details shape a seller that declares `execution_requirements` MUST use for a `VALIDATION_ERROR` returned because a buyer-supplied package does not satisfy an `event_source` or `catalog` entry in its product's `execution_requirements`. Unmet `downstream_connection` requirements use `AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED` with `error-details/authorization-required.json` instead. `error.field` names the first unmet binding; `unmet_requirements[]` lists every unmet requirement found. A seller that also emits `issues[]` SHOULD emit one entry per unmet requirement, in the same order.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "unmet_requirements": [
        {
          "field": "packages[0].optimization_goals",
          "product_id": "social_conversions_feed",
          "reason": "not_bound",
          "requirement": {
            "event_types": [
              "purchase"
            ],
            "kind": "event_source"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "properties": {
    "unmet_requirements": {
      "items": {
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "properties": {
          "field": {
            "description": "Request path where the resource binds, in the same JSONPath-lite form as `error.field`: `packages[i].optimization_goals` or `packages[i].catalogs` on `create_media_buy`; `new_packages[i].\u2026` or `packages[i].\u2026` on `update_media_buy`. For `not_found` and `ineligible`, sellers SHOULD point at the offending entry (for example `packages[0].optimization_goals[1].event_sources[0]` or `packages[0].catalogs[0]`).",
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "product_id": {
            "description": "Product whose requirement is unmet.",
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string",
            "x-entity": "product"
          },
          "reason": {
            "description": "`not_bound`: the package does not reference a resource of this kind. `not_found`: the referenced resource is not available to the account (for example an `event_source_id` that was never registered through `sync_event_sources`); register or sync it, then retry. `ineligible`: the referenced resource exists but does not satisfy the requirement (for example an event type or catalog type the requirement does not list).",
            "enum": [
              "not_bound",
              "not_found",
              "ineligible"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "requirement": {
            "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
            "description": "The product's declared requirement, echoed so the buyer can fix the request without another `get_products` call.",
            "discriminator": {
              "propertyName": "kind"
            },
            "examples": [
              {
                "catalog_types": [
                  "app"
                ],
                "kind": "catalog"
              }
            ],
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "description": "Each package needs a catalog. Satisfied by a `packages[].catalogs[]` entry whose `type` is in `catalog_types`. App promotion uses `[\"app\"]`; app items carry `app_id`, `bundle_id`, `apple_id`, and `store_url`. Every listed type MUST also appear in the product's `catalog_types`.",
                "properties": {
                  "catalog_types": {
                    "description": "Catalog types that satisfy the requirement (any-of). One catalog of any listed type satisfies it.",
                    "items": {
                      "enum": [
                        "app",
                        "job",
                        "hotel",
                        "store",
                        "flight",
                        "product",
                        "vehicle",
                        "offering",
                        "education",
                        "inventory",
                        "promotion",
                        "destination",
                        "real_estate"
                      ]
                    },
                    "maxItems": 13,
                    "minItems": 1,
                    "type": "array",
                    "uniqueItems": true
                  },
                  "ext": {
                    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
                    "description": "Extension object for platform-specific, vendor-namespaced parameters. Extensions are always optional and must be namespaced under a vendor/platform key (e.g., ext.gam, ext.roku). Used for custom capabilities, partner-specific configuration, and features being proposed for standardization.",
                    "title": "Extension Object",
                    "type": "object"
                  },
                  "kind": {
                    "const": "catalog"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "catalog_types",
                  "kind"
                ],
                "title": "Catalog Execution Requirement",
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "description": "Each package needs event optimization fed by a conversion event source; declare it only when the product requires event optimization. Satisfied when an `optimization_goals[]` entry of `kind: \"event\"` that the seller will use has a used `event_sources[]` entry referencing an event source available to the account (registered via `sync_event_sources`, or the seller-managed source it returns under `conversion_tracking.platform_managed: true`) with an `event_type` accepted here.",
                "properties": {
                  "event_types": {
                    "description": "Event types that satisfy the requirement (any-of): the satisfying `event_sources[]` entry MUST use one of these `event_type` values. Omit when any event type satisfies it.",
                    "items": {
                      "enum": [
                        "lead",
                        "share",
                        "custom",
                        "donate",
                        "follow",
                        "refund",
                        "search",
                        "contact",
                        "purchase",
                        "schedule",
                        "page_view",
                        "subscribe",
                        "app_launch",
                        "add_to_cart",
                        "app_install",
                        "select_item",
                        "start_trial",
                        "viewed_cart",
                        "content_view",
                        "qualify_lead",
                        "view_content",
                        "select_content",
                        "add_to_wishlist",
                        "disqualify_lead",
                        "watch_milestone",
                        "add_payment_info",
                        "remove_from_cart",
                        "initiate_checkout",
                        "close_convert_lead",
                        "submit_application",
                        "complete_registration"
                      ]
                    },
                    "maxItems": 31,
                    "minItems": 1,
                    "type": "array",
                    "uniqueItems": true
                  },
                  "ext": {
                    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
                    "description": "Extension object for platform-specific, vendor-namespaced parameters. Extensions are always optional and must be namespaced under a vendor/platform key (e.g., ext.gam, ext.roku). Used for custom capabilities, partner-specific configuration, and features being proposed for standardization.",
                    "title": "Extension Object",
                    "type": "object"
                  },
                  "kind": {
                    "const": "event_source"
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "kind"
                ],
                "title": "Event Source Execution Requirement",
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "description": "The product needs a seller-side platform connection or grant, such as the advertiser account or the publisher identity the ads run as. Satisfied by completing the connection, not by a request field; a missing, pending, expired, or revoked connection fails with `AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED` per `error-details/authorization-required.json`. A connection needed by every package MUST be declared here; one needed only by some formats stays in that format declaration's `required_connections`. With several eligible connected identities, the seller applies its documented default.",
                "properties": {
